@startuml reader
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members
title Reader base — dominio, servicio y servidor Python

package "Core (sin HTTP ni hardware)" {
  class ReaderCore {
    +reader_id: str
    +allow_new_devices: bool = True
    +allow_new_sensors: bool = True
    +on_register_device: Callable(Device)
    +on_observation: Callable(Observation)
    +register_device(device)
    +add_device(device)
    +get_device(device_id)
    +remove_device(device_id)
    +create_observation(device_id, sensor_id, value, phenomenon_time)
    +ingest(observation, send=True): bool
    +send_observation(observation)
  }
  class Device {
    +device_id: str
    +device_type: str
    +platform: str
    +add_sensor(sensor)
    +get_sensor(sensor_id)
    +remove_sensor(sensor_id)
    +list_sensors()
  }
  class Sensor {
    +sensor_id: str
    +device_id: str
    +observable_property: str
    +procedure: str
    +feature_of_interest: str
    +unit: str
    +build_observation(raw_value, phenomenon_time)
  }
  class Observation {
    +observation_id: str
    +device_id: str
    +sensor_id: str
    +observable_property: str
    +simple_result: Any
    +phenomenon_time: datetime
    +feature_of_interest: str
    +procedure: str
    +unit: str
  }
}
package "Service y outputs" {
  class ReaderService {
    +ingest(observation): bool
    +register_device_output(device)
    +publish(observation)
    +metadata(stream_enabled=False)
    +devices()
  }
  interface ObservationOutput {
    +register_device(reader_id, device)
    +publish(reader_id, observation)
  }
  class StreamOutput
  class ObservationStream {
    +subscribe()
    +publish(event)
    +close()
  }
  class "Serialización JSON" as JSON {
    +observation_to_dict(observation)
    +observation_event(reader_id, observation)
  }
}
package "Server HTTP opcional" {
  class ReaderServer {
    +start()
    +stop()
    +status()
    +app
  }
  class ServerConfig {
    +enabled: bool = False
    +host: str = 127.0.0.1
    +port: int = 3002
    +token: str
    +stream_enabled: bool = True
    +queue_size: int = 256
  }
}
ReaderCore o-- "0..*" Device : registro local
Device o-- "0..*" Sensor
Sensor ..> Observation : construye
ReaderCore ..> Observation : valida y emite el objeto
ReaderService --> ReaderCore : core externo
ReaderCore --> ReaderService : callbacks instalados por el servicio
ReaderService o-- "0..*" ObservationOutput : distribuye objetos
StreamOutput ..|> ObservationOutput
StreamOutput --> JSON
StreamOutput --> ObservationStream
ReaderServer *-- ReaderService : compone
ReaderServer --> ReaderCore : recibe instancia externa
ReaderServer --> ServerConfig
ReaderServer --> ObservationStream
ReaderServer ..> StreamOutput : añade si stream habilitado
note bottom of ReaderCore
  on_observation puede ser una función del usuario.
  Si se conecta ReaderService, este gestiona los callbacks.
  Core no serializa ni envía HTTP por sí mismo.
end note
note bottom of ReaderServer
  GET /health, /metadata, /devices
  GET /observations/stream (opcional)
  No existe ingestión HTTP ni historial SSE.
  enabled refleja el código actual: aún no se ha eliminado.
end note
@enduml
